  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the ground beef and cook, breaking it up with a spoon, until browned, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the onion and garlic and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Stir in the beef broth, water, black pepper, and sugar; bring to a boil.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, for 10 minutes.",
    "Stir in the lacquer glaze and mustard.",
    "Season with salt and pepper to taste.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with chopped fresh parsley or dill, if desired.",
    "Cook ground beef to an internal temperature of 71°C / 160°F."
